  "notes": "{整|ととの}える is a transitive verb ({他動詞|たどうし}) meaning to put things in proper order.\n\nINTRANSITIVE PAIR: {整|ととの}う (to be arranged, to be ready)\n- {整|ととの}える: I arrange the room.\n- {整|ととの}う: The preparations are complete.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{整|ととの}えている indicates the arranging process is ongoing.\n\nPARTICLE PATTERNS:\n- [thing]を{整|ととの}える — to arrange/prepare [thing]\n- [condition]を{整|ととの}える — to regulate/condition [condition]\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {身|み}だしなみを{整|ととの}える (groom oneself)\n- {環境|かんきょう}を{整|ととの}える (prepare the environment)\n- {呼吸|こきゅう}を{整|ととの}える (regulate breathing)\n- {体調|たいちょう}を{整|ととの}える (condition one's health)\n\nSAUNA CULTURE:\n{整|ととの}う has become popular in sauna culture, referring to the blissful state achieved after alternating hot and cold bathing.",
